from pathlib import Path
import json,html,hashlib,datetime
O=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
rows=json.loads((O/'scores_all72.json').read_text())
# Literature summaries describe source results; 'application' is a proposed use here.
entries=[
('Binary completion','Pay only for a successful sit and hold. Simple target, but early learning can receive little guidance.','Hindsight Experience Replay,2017','https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.01495','Keep a clear completion bonus. Sparse reward alone is unlikely to fix rare landing slips.'),
('Dense weighted components','Add small rewards for useful posture/contact and penalties for slip, hard impact and effort. Weights can create unwanted tradeoffs.','PhysHSI,2025 preprint','https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.11072','Retain completion dominance. Make worsening slip distinguishable after crossing the threshold; do not let effort savings compensate contact failures.'),
('Progress-based shaping','Reward improvement toward a goal rather than merely remaining near it. Potential-based shaping preserves optimal policies under its stated assumptions.','Ng, Harada & Russell,1999','https://ai.stanford.edu/~ang/papers/shaping-icml99.pdf','Use progress toward legal supported rest; define terminal potentials correctly. This does not guarantee fast learning with our neural policy.'),
('Stage-specific or gated rewards','Give different guidance for approaching, making contact and settling. Only enable comfort/effort rewards when the relevant contact conditions hold.','WoCoCo,CoRL2024 proceedings2025','https://proceedings.mlr.press/v270/zhang25a.html','A phase-aware approach/contact/hold objective is a substantive alternative to one global weighted sum.'),
('Demonstration tracking','Reward matching successful example poses, velocities and contacts. Hierarchies can combine reusable example motions.','Learning to Sit,AAAI2021','https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/16736','Provide successful sitting/leaning examples, retargeted to this robot. Fixed-frame tracking can constrain adaptation to new surfaces.'),
('Learned motion-style reward','A discriminator learns what plausible scene interactions look like; combine this with task completion.','Synthesizing Physical Character-Scene Interactions,SIGGRAPH2023','https://xbpeng.github.io/projects/InterPhys/index.html','Use diverse contact-aware examples to guide exploration. Style does not itself certify no slipping or forbidden contacts.'),
('Separate reward and constraints','Optimize task reward while explicitly constraining harmful outcomes instead of mixing everything into one score.','Constrained Policy Optimization,ICML2017','https://proceedings.mlr.press/v70/achiam17a.html','Treat protected-case retention as an explicit evaluation requirement. Expected-cost constraints are not guarantees for every individual case.'),
('Risk-sensitive or worst-case emphasis','Give more importance to rare bad outcomes or the poorly performing tail instead of only the average.','Chow et al.,2017','https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.01629','Prioritize recurring failure conditions and measure worst-case retention. Tail estimates require sufficient samples.'),
('Human preference reward','Learn a reward from people comparing short behavior clips.','Deep RL from Human Preferences,2017','https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.03741','Useful for comfort/naturalness or acceptable settling. Keep measured safety checks separate; tiny slips can be invisible to people.'),
('Automated reward search','Search over reward programs using measured training performance and feedback.','Eureka,ICLR2024','https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.12931','Use a bounded, reproducible search with independent selection criteria. It consumes experiments and can exploit poorly specified metrics; not an automatic fix.'),
('Goal-conditioned rewards and hindsight','Express different desired outcomes as goals; replay achieved goals to learn from unsuccessful attempts.','Hindsight Experience Replay,2017','https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.01495','Potentially useful across seats and support locations, but standard HER needs an off-policy learner. It is not a drop-in addition to the current PPO update.')]
meta={'utc':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),'scope':'Targeted primary-literature scan; principal practical families and combinations, not an exhaustive list of all possible reward formulas.','reward_families':[dict(family=e[0],source_summary=e[1],paper=e[2],url=e[3],application_proposed=e[4]) for e in entries],
'current_problem':'Reference-assisted residual PPO can adjust three symmetric pitch channels by at most0.004rad (~0.23deg), with0.004rad/s slew. It is learning small corrections to a preset low-seat sitting controller. This comparison does not validate general leaning.',
'evidence_vs_hypothesis':{'measured':'Revised seed63111 checkpoint64:59/72 strict clean,70stable,13slipping,2forbidden contacts. Eight original failures and five regressions.','local_optimum':'Possible but unproven; plateau and failures alone do not establish local optimality.','PPO_unsuitable':'Not established. PhysHSI uses PPO for humanoid interaction, with substantially different action freedom, data and training design.','earlier_causal_explanation':'Training coverage, exploration/evaluation mismatch and flat severity shaping are supported concerns, not experimentally isolated causes.'},
'criteria':{'full_horizon_s':20,'final_continuous_qualifying_hold_s':5,'strict_score':'1 only if stable completion, no physical failure, zero slip_ticks and zero illegal_ticks;0otherwise.','loaded_contact_force_threshold':'force norm >1%bodyweight','slip_fail':'loaded contact tangential speed >0.02m/s at any20ms sample','rest_load_minimum':'normal support load >=5%bodyweight','qualifying_hold_limits':'root speed <=0.10m/s;angular speed <=0.25rad/s;trunk tilt <=40deg;friction utilization <=0.90;legal contacts,joint margin,latched alive required.','physical_failures':'fall(root height<0.28m or tilt>55deg),forbidden contact(wrong contact force>10N or active contact outside permitted patch),torque limit,impact>2bodyweights,joint-limit margin violation.','reward_is_not_success_score':True,'criteria_unchanged':True},
'perfectionism':'The current metric is stricter than a visual successful-sit judgment: a single20ms slip fails the entire trial. Preserve the declared metric, but report stable completion, slip severity/duration, and forbidden contacts separately. Whether brief controlled settling should be acceptable is a task-definition decision, not a reward hack.',
'closest_robotics_example':{'paper':'PhysHSI,2025 preprint','url':'https://arxiv.org/html/2510.11072v1','reported_real_robot_sitting':'9/10 trials','success_definition':'Base within0.1m of target with heading aligned; paper specifies15degree angular tolerance.','method':'PPO with task,regularization and learned motion-style rewards;29joint outputs.','comparison_limit':'Different robot/task/distribution and success criteria; cannot compare its90% directly with our81.9%strict score.'},
'next_step_recommendation':['Finish128comparison unchanged.','First compare retention-aware sampling across all72development cases against current sampling at matched total budget.','Then test one smooth slip-severity reward ablation while preserving clean-success ranking.','If unchanged failures persist, review the3-channel residual controller and frozen reference; consider demonstration-guided,stage-conditioned control rather than endless weight tuning. A different controller requires a separately specified and authorized experiment.'],
'no_launch_or_training_change':True}
(O/'literature_review.json').write_text(json.dumps(meta,indent=2)+'\n')
E=html.escape
cols=[('case','Case'),('classification','Group'),('strict_score','Strict score /1'),('stable_hold_pass','Stable completion'),('final_hold_s','Final hold(s)'),('slip_duration_s','Slip(s)'),('peak_loaded_slip_m_s','Peak slip(cm/s)'),('forbidden_contact','Forbidden contact'),('revised_training_return','Learning return')]
def table(rr):
 s='<table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+v+'</th>' for k,v in cols)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'
 for r in rr:
  s+='<tr>'
  for k,_ in cols:
   v=r[k]
   if k=='peak_loaded_slip_m_s':v=f'{v*100:.4f}'
   elif isinstance(v,bool):v='yes' if v else 'no'
   elif isinstance(v,float):v=f'{v:.3f}'
   s+='<td>'+E(str(v))+'</td>'
  s+='</tr>'
 return s+'</tbody></table>'
failed=[r for r in rows if not r['strict_score']]
research='<table><thead><tr><th>Reward family</th><th>What research does</th><th>What it could mean here</th></tr></thead><tbody>'
for family,summary,paper,url,application in entries:research+=f'<tr><td><b>{E(family)}</b></td><td>{E(summary)} <a href="{url}">{E(paper)}</a></td><td>{E(application)}</td></tr>'
research+='</tbody></table>'
doc='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Sitting: evidence, failure video and reward options</title><style>body{font:16px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif;background:#f3f6f8;color:#183347;margin:32px auto;max-width:1300px;padding:0 24px}h1{font-size:32px}h2{margin-top:36px}video{width:100%;background:#132631;border-radius:12px}a{color:#075f9d}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;background:white;font-size:14px}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid #dae4ec;padding:10px}th{background:#dfeaf1}p{max-width:1100px}.box{background:white;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #d29632;border-radius:8px}.small{color:#506878;font-size:14px}</style><h1>What is actually failing?</h1><p><b>Most attempts reach a stable sit. Our current problem is eliminating brief slips and two forbidden hip-housing contacts without spoiling the successful cases.</b> The current PPO experiment learns tiny corrections to a preset sitting routine; it does not yet train unrestricted whole-body sitting or leaning.</p><p>The counts below were independently checked against saved measurements. A local optimum is possible, but has not been demonstrated. Neither reward coefficients nor PPO itself has been established as the sole cause.</p><div class="box"><b>Revised rewards / seed63111 /64updates:</b>59/72 strict clean(81.9%);70/72 stable(97.2%);13slipping;2forbidden contacts. Categories overlap. Baseline64/72clean(88.9%). No original failing case repaired.</div><h2>46-second failure replay</h2><video controls preload="metadata" src="failing_cases_revised64_v2.mp4"></video><p class="small">All13 failed cases, plus one clearly labeled clean reference. Two pages each show full20-second trials at1x. This is a schematic replay of recorded simulation poses, not camera footage or a new simulation. Pose samples are100ms apart; the graphs use all20ms contact measurements. Training was not interrupted.</p><h2>What does a score mean?</h2><p><b>Strict score1:</b> complete20seconds, finish with5continuous seconds of qualifying supported rest, and have no slipping, forbidden contact, fall, hard impact or joint/torque-limit violation anywhere in the trial. Otherwise score0. A loaded contact moving faster than2cm/s for even one20ms sample fails the zero-slip criterion. The separate learning return is a weighted training signal, not a percentage or pass score.</p><p>Qualifying rest requires at least5%bodyweight of normal support load, low root speed(≤0.10m/s), low angular speed(≤0.25rad/s), trunk tilt≤40°, legal contact and friction/joint margins. Unwanted body contact above10N is a physical failure. Full formulas and checks are recorded in the accompanying JSON.</p><h2>Each failed attempt</h2>'''+table(failed)+'''<p><a href="scores_all72.csv">Download all72 scores(CSV)</a> · <a href="scores_all72.json">Full measurements(JSON)</a> · <a href="video_manifest.json">Video provenance and checks</a></p><details><summary>Show every attempt, including all59 successes</summary>'''+table(rows)+'''</details><h2>Are we being too strict?</h2><p>Partly: a visually stable sit with a20ms slip receives the same binary fail label as a serious contact failure. We should retain the current metric while also showing severity and task completion. Whether controlled settling is acceptable needs an explicit task-definition decision. For context, <a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2510.11072v1">PhysHSI</a> reports9/10real-robot sitting trials with position/orientation-based completion criteria, not our whole-trial zero-slip rule. Its result is not directly comparable.</p><h2>Research-backed reward choices</h2><p>This targeted scan covers the main practical families; there are infinitely many weightings and combinations. Applications below are proposals for this project, not experimentally validated fixes.</p>'''+research+'''<h2>Training choices beyond the reward</h2><p>Demonstrations, staged approach/contact/hold training, varied surfaces and starts, exposure to all protected cases, and appropriate exploration can matter as much as the formula. <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.11072">PhysHSI</a> combines PPO with learned motion style, task rewards and regularization; its29-joint control is much broader than our three bounded correction channels. <a href="https://proceedings.mlr.press/v270/zhang25a.html">WoCoCo</a> breaks difficult whole-body contact tasks into stages.</p><h2>Recommendation</h2><p>Finish the128-update experiment unchanged. Next, test broader protected-case sampling, then a separate smooth slip-severity reward change. If the same failures persist, review the frozen reference and restricted controller, and prepare a demonstration-guided,stage-conditioned alternative. Do not endlessly tune rewards or declare PPO unsuitable from this one comparison.</p><p class="small">Local optimum, noise causality and the need for larger action authority remain unproven. No new training, simulator replay or holdout access occurred. <a href="literature_review.json">Research and criteria record</a>.</p></html>'''
(O/'review.html').write_text(doc)
print(json.dumps({'report':str(O/'review.html'),'reward_families':len(entries),'failed_scores':len(failed),'all_scores':len(rows)}))
